// ============================================================================
// Projections · CONFIG (.properties)  (pure column views — no joins, no closures)
//
// Named views over .properties config (application.properties, etc.), for both the
// client (java_*) and any external library (lib_*). Config-driven wiring: a value
// may name a class (x.class=com.example.Y), and property references (${...}) link
// keys together and across services. Interpretation (class-name -> type, grouping
// placeholders) is a resolution-layer step.
//
// Conventions: views only; one raw base relation per rule body; provenance tag first.
//
// java_property_key cols (14):
//   0 key  1 rawKey  2 delimiter  3 hasValue  4 isMultiLineKey  5 isMultiLineValue
//   6 filePath  7 baseMservPath  8 startLine  9 endLine  10 startColumn
//   11 endColumn  12 serviceVersionLinkHash  13 propertyKeyUniqueHash
//
// java_property_value_segment cols (12):
//   0 segmentValue  1 segmentType  2 defaultValue  3 position  4 depth
//   5 parentSegmentLinkHash  6 propertyKeyLinkHash  7 startLine  8 endLine
//   9 startColumn  10 endColumn  11 propertyValueSegmentUniqueHash
// ============================================================================

// ── prop_key(Prov, Key, HasValue, FilePath, KeyHash) ────────────────────────
// A property key, whether it has a value, and its file.
prop_key("client", key, hasValue, filePath, h) :- java_property_key(key, _, _, hasValue, _, _, filePath, _, _, _, _, _, _, h).

// ── prop_segment(Prov, KeyHash, SegmentValue, SegmentType, DefaultValue, ParentSegmentHash, SegHash) ──
// One segment of a property value. A LITERAL segment may be a class name; a
// PROPERTY_REFERENCE / ENV_VARIABLE segment links to another key / env var.
//
// SegmentType (col 1, PropertyValueSegmentType enum):
//   LITERAL                    plain text (may name a class)
//   ENV_VARIABLE               ${ENV}
//   ENV_WITH_DEFAULT           ${ENV:default}
//   PROPERTY_REFERENCE         ${other.key}
//   PROPERTY_REF_WITH_DEFAULT  ${other.key:default}
//   SPEL_EXPRESSION            #{...} Spring EL
//   RANDOM                     ${random...}
//   EMPTY                      empty segment
prop_segment("client", keyHash, value, segType, default, parentSeg, h) :- java_property_value_segment(value, segType, default, _, _, parentSeg, keyHash, _, _, _, _, h).
